L156: \nL157: To Reproduce\nL158:   1. Configure two Supabase MCP servers with unique names (e.g., \"Supabase-RSX\" and \"Supabase-FMMS\")\nL159:   2. Both MCPs have the same command/args structure, only differing in `--project-ref`\nL160:   3. Prompt: \"Use Supabase-RSX to check current tables\"\nL161:   4. Kimi Code incorrectly uses \"Supabase-FMMS\" instead\nL162: \nL163: Expected behavior\nL164: Kimi Code should correctly reference the MCP specified by its unique name (e.g., \"Supabase-RSX\").\nL165: \nL166: Environment\nL167:   * Kimi Code version: 1.8.0\nL168:   * Platform: VSCode extension (issue not present in Kimi CLI)\nL169: Configuration Example\nL170: The MCPs share the same command/args structure, differing only in `--project-ref`:\nL171: \nL172:     {\nL173:       \"mcpServers\": {\nL174:         \"Supabase-RSX\": {\nL175:           \"command\": \"npx\",\nL176:           \"args\": [\nL177:             \"-y\",\nL178:             \"@supabase/mcp-server-supabase@latest\",\nL179:             \"--project-ref=<project-id>\"\nL180:           ],\nL181:           \"env\": {\nL182:             \"SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN\": \"<token>\"\nL183:           }\nL184:         },\nL185:         \"Supabase-FMMS\": {\nL186:           \"command\": \"npx\",\nL187:           \"args\": [\nL188:             \"-y\",\nL189:             \"@supabase/mcp-server-supabase@latest\",\nL190:             \"--project-ref=<project-id>\"\nL191:           ],\nL192:           \"env\": {\nL193:             \"SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN\": \"<token>\"\nL194:           }\nL195:         }\nL196:       }\nL197:     }\nL198: Additional context\nL199: \nL200:   * The only differences between the two MCPs are their names and `--project-ref` values\nL201:   * Kimi CLI correctly references the specified MCP\nL202:   * The issue appears specific to the Kimi Code VSCode extension\nL203: \nL204: Reactions are currently unavailable\nL205: ## Activity\nL206: \nL207: to join this conversation on GitHub. Already have an account? cite73†Sign in to comment L208: \nL209: ## Metadata\nL210: \nL211: ## Metadata\nL212: \nL213: ### Assignees\nL214: \nL215: No one assigned\nL216: \nL217: ### Labels\nL218: \nL219: No labels\nL220: \nL221: No labels\nL222: \nL223: ### Type\nL224: \nL225: No type\nL226: \nL227: ### Projects\nL228: \nL229: No projects\nL230: \nL231: ### Milestone\nL232: \nL233: No milestone\nL234: \nL235: ### Relationships\nL236: \nL237: None yet\nL238: \nL239: ### Development\nL240: \nL241: No branches or pull requests\nL242: \nL243: ## Issue actions\nL244: \nL245:   * cite74†Image†github.githubassets.com Open in GitHub Copilot app\nL246: \nL247: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLLM-discovered 0 days \\ Anthropic (https://www.anthropic.com/research/zero-days)\nciteturn31581view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.anthropic.com/research/zero-days\",\"pattern\":\"Update\"}); Total lines: 128\nNo matching text found for \"Update\"--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2602.08007v1] From $O(mn)$ to $O(r^2)$: Two-Sided Low-Rank Communication for Adam in Distributed Training with Memory Efficiency (https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.08007v1)\nciteturn31581view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.08007v1\",\"pattern\":\"Abstract\"}); Total lines: 165\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Machine Learning\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 8 Feb 2026]\nL9: # Title:From $O(mn)$ to $O(r^2)$: Two-Sided Low-Rank Communication for Adam in Distributed Training with Memory Efficiency\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Sizhe Dang , cite6†Jiaqi Shao , cite7†Xiaodong Zheng , cite8†Guang Dai , cite9†Yan Song , cite10†Haishan Ye L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled From $O(mn)$ to $O(r^2)$: Two-Sided Low-Rank Communication for Adam in Distributed Training with Memory Efficiency, by Sizhe Dang and 4 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite11†View PDF cite12†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:As foundation models continue to scale, pretraining increasingly relies on data-parallel distributed optimization, making bandwidth-limited gradient synchronization a key bottleneck. Orthogonally, projection-based low-rank optimizers were mainly designed for memory efficiency, but remain suboptimal for communication-limited training: one-sided synchronization still transmits an $O(rn)$ object for an $m\\times n$ matrix gradient and refresh steps can dominate peak communicated bytes.\nL17: We propose TSR, which brings two-sided low-rank communication to Adam-family updates (TSR-Adam) by synchronizing a compact core $U^\\top G V\\in\\mathbb{R}^{r\\times r}$, reducing the dominant per-step payload from $O(mn)$ to $O(r^2)$ while keeping moment states in low-dimensional cores. To further reduce the peak communication from subspace refresh, TSR-Adam adopts a randomized SVD-based refresh that avoids full-gradient synchronization.\nL18: We additionally extend low-rank communication to embedding gradients with embedding-specific ranks and refresh schedules, yielding additional communication and memory savings over keeping embeddings dense. Across pretraining from 60M to 1B model scales, TSR-Adam reduces average communicated bytes per step by $13\\times$, and on GLUE fine-tuning it reduces communication by $25\\times$, while achieving comparable performance; we further provide a theoretical stationarity analysis for the proposed update.\nL19: Code is available at cite13†this https URL†github.com .\nL20: Subjects:  | Machine Learning (cs.LG); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL21: Cite as:  | cite14†arXiv:2602.08007 [cs.LG]\nL22:    | (or cite15†arXiv:2602.08007v1 [cs.LG] for this version)\nL23:    | cite16†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2602.08007†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Sizhe Dang [cite17†view email ]\nL27: [v1] Sun, 8 Feb 2026 15:23:09 UTC (6,090 KB)\nL28: \nL29: Full-text links:\nL30: \nL31: ## Access Paper:\nL32: \nL33: View a PDF of the paper titled From $O(mn)$ to $O(r^2)$: Two-Sided Low-Rank Communication for Adam in Distributed Training with Memory Efficiency, by Sizhe Dang and 4 other authors\nL34: \nL35:   * cite11†View PDF L36:   * cite12†HTML (experimental) L37:   * cite18†TeX Source L38: \nL39: cite19†view license L40: ### Current browse context:\nL41: \nL42: cs.LG\nL43: \nL44: cite20†< prev |   cite21†next > L45: \nL46: cite22†new | cite23†recent | cite24†2026-02 L47: \nL48: Change to browse by:\nL49: \nL50: cite25†cs L51: cite26†cs.AI L52: \nL53: ### References & Citations\nL54: \nL55:   * cite27†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L56:   * cite28†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L57:   * cite29†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L58: \nL59: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL60: \nL61: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL62: \nL63: [Button: ×]\nL64: \nL65: loading...\nL66: \nL67: Data provided by:\nL68: \nL69: ### Bookmark\nL70: \nL71: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL72: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL73: \nL74: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL75: \nL76: Bibliographic Explorer (cite30†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org )\nL77: \nL78: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL79: \nL80: Connected Papers (cite31†What is Connected Papers?†www.connectedpapers.com )\nL81: \nL82: [Input] Litmaps Toggle\nL83: \nL84: Litmaps (cite32†What is Litmaps?†www.litmaps.co )\nL85: \nL86: [Input] scite.ai Toggle\nL87: \nL88: scite Smart Citations (cite33†What are Smart Citations?†www.scite